# Business-analyst baseline

While this plugin is installed, apply this gate before shaping or planning.
Depth lives in `business-analyst-when`, `business-analyst-brief`, and the
skills — do not copy those rules here.

## Stay out

If `business-analyst-when` stay-out matches (question answered by the repo,
label/copy tweak, single-field config, bug whose acceptance is "the failing
check passes", or work the user already scoped), do **not** write a brief or
lock a plan. Implement.

## Engage the brief

When the ask is a new capability, an unclear "what should we build", or a
story with no testable outcome yet:

1. Write the brief sections from `business-analyst-brief` in the parent turn
   before implementation edits.
2. On Full-tier or still-vague asks, you may launch agent `business-analyst`
   instead of writing the brief inline — same section list.
3. Ask at most one true blocker. Everything else is a marked assumption and
   continues

## After the brief

- If sequence across subsystems is still unclear, or the user asked for a
  plan this turn → `business-analyst-planner`.
- Technical approach, touch map, and verification commands →
  a later implementation pass. Do not invent a second design here.
- External library or API contract the repo does not document →
  `business-analyst-researcher`.
